@ifnottex
@node Top
@top ETL Madness Flow API

This manual documents @strong{go-flowAPI}, the centralized HTTP REST API,
artifact repository, live Server-Sent Events (SSE) execution gateway, granular
pipeline ACL engine, and multi-database telemetry daemon for the ETL Madness
Flow ecosystem.

@menu
* Overview and Architecture::   Supported databases, RBAC/ACL model, and package layout.
* Invoking go-flowAPI::         Command-line flags, precedence, and password hashing.
* Configuration File::          Syntax and variables for @file{go-flow-api.env}.
* OS Services and Daemons::     systemd, OpenRC, SysVinit, FreeBSD/OpenBSD rc.d, launchd, and Windows SCM.
* REST API Overview::           Core endpoints for artifacts, execution, ACLs, crypto, and telemetry.
@end menu
@end ifnottex

@node Overview and Architecture
@chapter Overview and Architecture

@command{go-flowAPI} compiles as a zero-dependency pure-Go static binary
(@code{CGO_ENABLED=0}) embedding the @code{go-flow} pipeline execution engine
and relational drivers for Microsoft SQL Server / Azure SQL, PostgreSQL,
MySQL / MariaDB, SQLite, and Oracle.

Packages install isolated under @file{/opt/flow-api} on Unix platforms
(Linux, macOS, FreeBSD, and OpenBSD) and
@file{C:\Program Files\ETL Madness\Flow API\} on Windows so binaries and manuals
never conflict with system packages or with the @code{go-flow} CLI package
(@file{/opt/flow}).

By default (@code{-strict-acl=true}), non-admin (@code{non-all}) accounts have
zero access to @code{pipeline} artifacts or execution unless granted via
explicit @code{allow} rules in @code{dbo.flow_pipeline_acl}.

@command{go-flowAPI} does not auto-create database tables at startup. Before
starting the service against a new database, apply the schema DDL in
@file{/opt/flow-api/share/doc/SCHEMA.md} or the ready-to-run SQL scripts in
@file{/opt/flow-api/share/sql/}.

@node Invoking go-flowAPI
@chapter Invoking @command{go-flowAPI}

Synopsis:

@example
go-flowAPI [-env-file PATH] [-dsn URI] [-addr HOST:PORT] [options...]
go-flowAPI -hash-password "PlaintextPassword"
@end example

@section Command-Line Flags

@table @code
@item -dsn @var{URI}
Database connection string override (@env{FLOW_API_DSN}).
@item -addr @var{ADDR}
HTTP TCP listen address, default @code{:8080} (@env{FLOW_API_ADDR} or @env{PORT}).
@item -env-file @var{PATH}
Load unset @code{KEY=VALUE} environment variables from @var{PATH} (@env{FLOW_API_ENV_FILE}).
@item -log-file @var{PATH}
Append server log output to @var{PATH} (@env{FLOW_API_LOG_FILE}).
@item -service-name @var{NAME}
Windows SCM service name when running as a Windows Service (default @code{GoFlowAPI}).
@item -secure-key @var{KEY}
Default AES-256-GCM passphrase (@env{FLOW_SECURE_KEY}).
@item -key-file @var{PATH}
File containing the default AES-256-GCM passphrase.
@item -bootstrap-user @var{USER}
Seed or update an initial BasicAuth user at startup (@env{FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_USER}).
@item -bootstrap-pass @var{PASS}
Password for @code{-bootstrap-user}, automatically bcrypt-hashed (@env{FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_PASS}).
@item -bootstrap-perm @var{ROLE}
Permission role for @code{-bootstrap-user}: @code{all} (default), @code{scoped}, @code{execution-only}, @code{read-only}, @code{write}, or @code{upload}.
@item -strict-acl
Enforce strict ACL-only pipeline authorization so non-@code{all} users require explicit @code{dbo.flow_pipeline_acl} grants (default @code{true}; @env{FLOW_API_STRICT_ACL}).
@item -hash-password @var{PASS}
Print a bcrypt hash of @var{PASS} to stdout and exit.
@item -debug
Enable verbose debug logging (@env{FLOW_API_DEBUG}).
@end table

@node Configuration File
@chapter Environment Configuration (@file{go-flow-api.env})

Default file locations by platform:

@itemize @bullet
@item Linux and OpenBSD: @file{/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env}
@item FreeBSD: @file{/usr/local/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env}
@item macOS: @file{/opt/flow-api/etc/go-flow-api.env}
@item Windows: @file{C:\ProgramData\ETL Madness\Flow API\go-flow-api.env}
@end itemize

Key environment variables include @env{FLOW_API_DSN}, @env{FLOW_API_ADDR},
@env{FLOW_SECURE_KEY}, @env{FLOW_API_LOG_FILE}, @env{FLOW_API_STRICT_ACL},
@env{FLOW_API_DEBUG}, and Active Directory / Kerberos variables
(@env{AD_REALM}, @env{KRB5_CONFIG}, @env{KRB5_KTNAME}, @env{KRB5CCNAME},
@env{FLOW_WINDOWS_USER}, @env{FLOW_WINDOWS_GROUPS}, @env{FLOW_WINDOWS_GROUPS_FILE}).

@node OS Services and Daemons
@chapter Configuring OS Services and @code{rc} Scripts

@section Linux (@code{systemd})
Linux @code{.deb}, @code{.rpm}, and Arch @code{.pkg.tar.zst} packages create
the unprivileged @code{flowapi} user, install @file{/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env}
(mode @code{0640}), and register @file{/usr/lib/systemd/system/go-flow-api.service}:

@example
sudo vi /etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
sudo systemctl enable --now go-flow-api.service
sudo systemctl status go-flow-api.service
sudo journalctl -u go-flow-api.service -f
@end example

@section Linux (OpenRC and SysVinit)
For Alpine, Gentoo, Devuan, or SysVinit hosts, ready-to-install init scripts
are bundled under @file{/opt/flow-api/share/services/openrc/go-flow-api} and
@file{/opt/flow-api/share/services/sysvinit/go-flow-api}. Copy the appropriate
script to @file{/etc/init.d/go-flow-api} (@code{chmod 0755}) and enable via
@code{rc-update add go-flow-api default} (OpenRC) or @code{update-rc.d go-flow-api defaults}
/ @code{chkconfig --add go-flow-api} (SysVinit).

@section FreeBSD (@code{rc.d})
The FreeBSD @code{.pkg} installs @file{/usr/local/etc/rc.d/go_flow_api} and
seeds @file{/usr/local/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env}:

@example
sudo vi /usr/local/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
sudo sysrc go_flow_api_enable="YES"
sudo service go_flow_api start
sudo service go_flow_api status
@end example

@section OpenBSD (@code{rc.d} / @command{rcctl})
The OpenBSD @code{.tgz} installs @file{/etc/rc.d/go_flow_api}, creates the
@code{flowapi} daemon user, and seeds @file{/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env}:

@example
doas vi /etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
doas rcctl enable go_flow_api
doas rcctl start go_flow_api
doas rcctl check go_flow_api
@end example

@section macOS (@code{launchd})
Configure @file{/opt/flow-api/etc/go-flow-api.env} (@code{chmod 0600}), copy
@file{/opt/flow-api/share/services/launchd/com.etlmadness.go-flow-api.plist}
into @file{/Library/LaunchDaemons/}, and run:

@example
sudo launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.etlmadness.go-flow-api.plist
sudo launchctl kickstart -k system/com.etlmadness.go-flow-api
@end example

@section Windows (Native SCM Windows Service)
@file{go-flowAPI.exe} natively supports the Windows Service Control Manager.
Run the bundled PowerShell installer in an elevated Administrator shell:

@example
& "C:\Program Files\ETL Madness\Flow API\share\services\windows\Install-GoFlowAPIService.ps1" -Start
@end example

Pass @code{-Credential (Get-Credential "DOMAIN\svc_flowapi")} or
@code{-GroupManagedServiceAccount "DOMAIN\gmsa_flowapi$"} when connecting to
Microsoft SQL Server with Windows Integrated Authentication.

@node REST API Overview
@chapter REST API Overview

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{GET /api/v1/health}: Public health, database driver, caller groups, and schema check.
@item @code{GET /swagger/} and @code{GET /api/v1/openapi.json}: Interactive Swagger UI and OpenAPI 3.0.3 spec.
@item @code{/api/v1/artifacts/@{type@}} and @code{/api/v1/upload/@{type@}}: CRUD, ID lookup, XML export, and file upload for @code{pipelines}, @code{options}, and @code{configs}.
@item @code{POST /api/v1/execute}, @code{POST /api/v1/execute/stream}, @code{POST /api/v1/validate}: Synchronous execution, live SSE node streaming, and XSD/AST validation (including ID-based variants).
@item @code{/api/v1/crypto/*}: Keypair generation, AES-256-GCM encryption/decryption, and OpenSSL/PKCS#7/OpenPGP signing and verification.
@item @code{GET /api/v1/runs}, @code{GET /api/v1/events}, @code{GET /api/v1/audit}: Execution history, @code{node_output} telemetry, and API audit trail.
@item @code{/api/v1/users}, @code{/api/v1/groups}, @code{/api/v1/pipeline-groups}, @code{/api/v1/acls}, @code{GET /api/v1/permissions/effective}: Administrative user, group, pipeline-group, granular ACL management, and effective permissions simulator.
@item @code{POST /api/v1/db/test}: Administrative DSN connectivity verification.
@end itemize

